
# --- playbook commit template (docs/12 2, docs/16 4.1) ---
# Conventional Commits, written in English:
#   <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# type:  feat | fix | chore | docs | refactor | test | ci
# scope: docs | templates | harness | scripts | conventions | infra
# subject: imperative mood, <= ~72 chars, no trailing period ("add x", not "added x")
#
# Body (optional): explain the WHY (not the how), wrap at ~72 cols.
#
# Rules:
# - Author is nerdkim. Add the sanctioned co-author trailer below; never add any
#   OTHER co-author (e.g. Claude) or a generated signature.
# - No forbidden unicode (em dash / en dash / bullet ...); ASCII only (docs/16 2.1).
# - Docs and replies are Korean; code/comments/commit/PR are English (docs/16 4.1).
# - Standard change: bump VERSION when appropriate and note it in a GitHub Release.

